    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSherry FitzGerald is delighted to present 55 St Joseph's Place to the market.\n\nTucked away in a quiet residential enclave between Dorset Street Upper and Nelson Street, this charming redbrick mid-terrace cottage offers a wonderful opportunity to acquire a beautifully presented home in the heart of Dublin 7. Behind its attractive façade lies bright and airy accommodation enhanced by high ceilings, tasteful finishes and a private west-facing rear courtyard.\n\nThe well-appointed accommodation briefly comprises an entrance hall, a spacious living/dining room, kitchen, bathroom and double bedroom. To the rear, the enclosed courtyard provides a peaceful outdoor retreat, creating a private oasis just minutes from the city centre. A concrete block shed, plumbed and wired for electricity, offers excellent additional storage.\n\nThe location is second to none. The Mater Hospital is just moments away, while Dublin City Centre is within easy walking distance. The Broadstone Luas stop and several Dublin Bikes stations are close by, ensuring excellent connectivity throughout the city. Dublin Airport can be reached in approximately 20 minutes by car.\n\nResidents are spoiled by the wealth of amenities in the area, including the picturesque Blessington Basin and Royal Canal Greenway, complete with a playground and community garden. The TUD Grangegorman campus, St Patrick's Training College and the National Botanic Gardens are all within walking distance, while both the Phoenix Park and the Grand Canal are easily accessible. The vibrant village atmosphere of nearby Phibsborough and Drumcondra offers an excellent selection of shops, cafés, bars and restaurants, making this an exceptionally convenient and desirable place to call home."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance - \nSolid timber floor\n\nLiving Room - 5.65m x 5.15m\nBright and airy open plan layout with impressive high ceiling, solid timber floor and built in shelving units.\n\nKitchen - 2.95m x 3.47m\nFloor and eye level units, tiled splash back, solid timber floor and door to west facing courtyard.\n\nShower Room - 1.30m x 1.45m\nWc, whb and Triton shower\n\nBedroom - 2.90m x 2.87m\nDouble bedroom overlooking the courtyard\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>One-bedroom cottage</li><li>Well-proportioned accommodation</li><li>Tucked away in a quiet cul de sac</li><li>West facing courtyard </li><li>Convenient location close to city centre</li><li>Gas fired central heating.</li><li>TV & telephone points</li><li>Double glazed windows</ul>"
      },
